# DOCA CPU_PROXY support on top of izzy doca_rdma (pearl-izzy branch)
#
# Apply with:
#     cd /opt/doca_rdma_izzy && patch -p1 < .../01-cpu-proxy-mode.patch
#
# Summary
# - DBR backing memory: switch to plain calloc() when the user opts into
#   CPU_PROXY (env GLUE_RDMA_NIC_HANDLERS=1 + GLUE_RDMA_ALLOW_PROXY_HANDLERS=1),
#   matching DOCA sample verbs_high_level.c:375. CPU progress thread must
#   read/write the DBR record, so it cannot live in GPU memory.
# - New methods on DocaRdmaEndpoint:
#       cpu_proxy_enabled / cpu_proxy_progress / poll_send_cq_cpu
#   exposed through pybind. poll_send_cq_cpu decodes mlx5_err_cqe so test
#   harnesses can attribute REQ_ERR/RESP_ERR completions to a syndrome.
# - Kernel rdma_write_imm_kernel: when imm_value == 0, emit opcode 0x08
#   (RDMA_WRITE) instead of 0x09 (RDMA_WRITE_IMM). Lets us validate the
#   doorbell path without the responder needing a posted recv WR.
# - Replace post_recv stub with doca_verbs_bridge_post_recv (still broken
#   for external-datapath QPs; see follow-up task tracking).
# - Build fixes already in phase10 doc but consolidated here for one-shot
#   apply: ::listen namespace qualifier; CMakeLists pybind LTO off.

